# Spec–code parity (blocking)

This project uses **Spec-Driven Development** under `.specify/` and `.specify/memory/constitution.md` **v1.5.0+ Principle VII — Spec–code parity**.

## Before you finish any material change

If the change affects **any** of: HTTP contract, DTOs/OpenAPI shapes, domain rules, persistence/Flyway, queue/list/detail UX, acceptance criteria, ubiquitous language in user-facing text, or documented data model — you **MUST** update the matching feature artifacts **in the same change** (same commit or same PR with no spec drift left behind).

**Default feature root** (adjust if the user names another feature): `specs/001-mm-order-processing/`

| If you changed… | Update at least… |
|-----------------|------------------|
| REST paths, payloads, responses, errors | `contracts/openapi.yaml` → regenerate codegen as required; keep `contracts/api-v1.md` in lockstep (no contradiction) |
| Entities, fields, relationships | `data-model.md`; OpenAPI if exposed on the wire |
| User stories, behavior, AC, edge cases | `spec.md` |
| Architecture, tech stack, boundaries | `plan.md` |
| Task scope or done status | `tasks.md` |

## Stop conditions

- **Do not** present implementation as complete if only code (or only OpenAPI) changed but `spec.md`, `api-v1.md`, or `data-model.md` still describe the old behavior.
- If the user explicitly asks for “code only”, **refuse or warn** that this violates project SDD; offer to update the spec in the same pass or narrow the change to non-material refactors only.

## Exempt (no spec touch required)

Purely internal refactors with **zero** observable/API/DB/UX effect; comments-only; formatting. When uncertain, **update the spec**.

## Cross-reference

- Governance: `.specify/memory/constitution.md` Principle VII and **Amendment 1.5.0**
- Speckit workflows must treat missing spec sync as a failed gate
